{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1030756833/16/codegen_prompts/6.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1030756833/16`\n- 题号：`6`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1030756833/16/6.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"6\">\n- `description`：分析每个窗口内图案的对称性类型，通过色板区域的图标-颜色映射关系，将对称性类型转化为对应颜色重绘窗口边框。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为black。网格右下角有一个\"色板区域\"，由4列2行共8个像素构成。色板第一行（上方行）有四个不同颜色的像素（如red、blue、green、yellow）。色板第二行（下方行）对应位置分别是四种对称性的示意图标，每个图标为1个像素，颜色编排如下：\n    - 第1列下方像素左右对称着色，代表\"左右镜像对称\"，对应上方颜色。\n    - 第2列下方像素上下对称着色，代表\"上下镜像对称\"，对应上方颜色。\n    - 第3列下方像素为中心对称着色，代表\"旋转180度对称\"，对应上方颜色。\n    - 第4列下方像素为不对称着色，代表\"无对称性\"，对应上方颜色。\n  - 实际上，色板的对称性分类需要从训练样例中归纳：解题者通过观察多个样例中窗口图案与其边框被重绘的颜色之间的对应关系，反推色板中每列代表的对称性类型。\n  - 网格其余区域包含若干个由grey边框围成的正方形\"窗口\"（边框宽1像素，内部为奇数边长的正方形且至少3x3），窗口之间不重叠不相邻。\n  - 每个窗口内部有一个由某种非grey非black颜色绘制的图案。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 分析每个窗口内部图案的对称性：\n    - 若图案左右翻转后与原图案完全一致，则为\"左右镜像对称\"。\n    - 若图案上下翻转后与原图案完全一致（且不满足左右镜像），则为\"上下镜像对称\"。\n    - 若图案旋转180度后与原图案完全一致（且不满足任何单轴镜像），则为\"旋转180度对称\"。\n    - 若图案不满足以上任何对称性，则为\"无对称性\"。\n    - 若图案同时满足左右和上下镜像对称，归类为\"左右镜像对称\"（按优先级：左右 > 上下 > 旋转 > 无）。\n  - 从色板区域找到该对称性类型对应列的上方颜色。\n  - 将该窗口的grey边框全部重绘为该颜色。窗口内部图案保持不变。\n  - 色板区域本身保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要对每个窗口内的图案进行视觉对称性分析——在心中翻转或旋转图案来判断其对称类型。然后通过色板建立对称性类型到颜色的映射关系。色板中的图标本身编码了对称性类别，需要解题者从训练样例中归纳出图标含义，而非仅靠图标外观推断。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：train/e729b7be, train/3bd292e8, eval/4c416de3, train/f0f8a26d, eval/88e364bc, train/34cfa167, train/6350f1f4, eval/2c181942\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"e729b7be\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2922\nmechanism=0.3666\nlexical=0.0146\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:rotation, operation:parity, operation:reflect, operation:rotate, output:same_size, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/e729b7be.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/e729b7be.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nComplete the scene by adding the point-reflected copy of the colored object across the central marker.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has odd dimensions, a dominant background, and a center-row marker color appearing only at the left edge, center, and right edge.\n- A single divider color fills the center column except for the center marker.\n- All remaining foreground pixels form the object to copy, entirely on the left side of the divider.\nRule\n- Keep the input unchanged.\n- For every object pixel, paint the pixel rotated 180 degrees around the center marker with the same color.\nKey insight\n- The center marker is the rotation center; the yellow-looking divider is not mirrored, it only separates the source from the empty target side.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"symmetry/pattern\",\n  \"src\": \"colored foreground object pixels excluding the center-column divider and center-row markers\",\n  \"transform\": \"copy each source pixel to its 180-degree point-reflection through the center marker, preserving the original pixels, divider, and markers\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"3bd292e8\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2709\nmechanism=0.2758\nlexical=0.0171\ncode_feature=0.6667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:rotation, operation:reflect, output:same_size, relation:adjacent, relation:between, relation:direction\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/3bd292e8.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/3bd292e8.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRecolor wall-separated background regions alternately, starting with grey in the lower-left region.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has one dominant background color and one foreground wall color.\n- The wall pixels form one or more 4-connected one-cell-thick segments.\n- Each wall segment separates exactly two 4-connected background regions.\nRule\n- Keep all wall pixels unchanged.\n- Label the 4-connected background regions and connect two labels when they\n  touch opposite sides of the same wall segment.\n- Color the region containing the lower-left corner grey, then flip between\n  grey and green across every wall adjacency.\nKey insight\n- The red walls define a bipartite map of regions; the lower-left background\n  region fixes which side of the alternating coloring is grey.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"4-connected orange background regions separated by red one-cell-thick wall segments\",\n  \"transform\": \"keep red wall pixels; recolor the lower-left background region grey and recolor each wall-adjacent region with the opposite grey/green color\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"4c416de3\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2783\nmechanism=0.3556\nlexical=0.0114\ncode_feature=0.2857\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:rotation, object:frame, object:square, operation:reflect, operation:rotate, relation:between, relation:inside, relation:overlap\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/4c416de3.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/4c416de3.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nReplicate a pre-drawn corner pattern to every other marker-bearing corner.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most frequent color. Hollow 0-frames (possibly partial L-shapes); each\n  frame-corner cell is either 0 or a painted (non-bg, non-0) color.\n- >= 1 'source' corner: the pattern is already drawn (one color, both outward\n  cells and an inward-diagonal trail).\n- Other corners: a single colored pixel on the inward diagonal at the pattern's\n  deepest (k,k) offset; the pixel's color is that corner's target color.\n\nRule:\n- Extract the canonical (TL-oriented) pattern from any source.\n- For each non-source corner whose marker cell is colored, paint the same\n  pattern rotated to that corner's orientation, using the marker's color.\n\nKey insight: the pattern is symmetric about the corner's inward-diagonal axis\n(canonical dr == dc), so it reflects cleanly across all four corner orientations.\nPainting uses each target's OWN marker color, not the source color.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Colored sprites inside black hollow square frames move to match destination sprites inside other frames via various mirror/diagonal symmetries, with colors transferred\",\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"colored sprites s inside black hollow square frames, where anchor is defined as: 1) the sprite's inner pixel, and 2) the black pixel at the minimum corner of the square that overlaps with the sprite's inner pixel\",\n  \"dst\": \"single colored sprites d only inside black hollow square frames\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"symmetry(s.anchor) == d (various mirror and diagonal symmetries)\",\n  \"path\": \"\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"keep source\",\n  \"transform\": \"s.color -> d.color\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": null,\n  \"multi_step\": \"\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"mirror_symmetry\",\n    \"diagonal_symmetry\",\n    \"anchor_points\",\n    \"hollow_frames\",\n    \"color_transfer\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"Definition of anchor point: the relationship between sprite's inner pixel and the black pixel at minimum corner of square containing that pixel\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"f0f8a26d\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2840\nmechanism=0.3263\nlexical=0.0106\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:rotation, operation:parity, operation:reflect, operation:rotate, output:same_size, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/f0f8a26d.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/f0f8a26d.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRotate every foreground bar 90 degrees around its own center on the same canvas.\n\nInput structure\nThe background is the dominant color, and all foreground pixels share one color.\nEach 4-connected foreground object is a solid one-cell-thick horizontal or vertical\nbar with odd length, with single-pixel bars allowed.\n\nRule\nClear the canvas to the background, then redraw every bar with its midpoint, length,\nand color preserved while swapping horizontal and vertical orientation.\n\nKey insight\nThe bars are independent objects: their centers and lengths identify the output\nplacement, so no matching, ordering, or global symmetry is needed.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"4-connected monochromatic foreground bars on a dominant background\",\n  \"transform\": \"rotate each odd-length horizontal or vertical bar 90 degrees about its midpoint; preserve its color and length, with single-pixel bars unchanged\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"88e364bc\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2418\nmechanism=0.2500\nlexical=0.0163\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:closed_region, object:frame, relation:adjacent, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/88e364bc.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/88e364bc.json\n</paths>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
